# ==============================================================================
# Sender-Dependent Outbound VIP Mapping (/etc/postfix/sender_transport)
# Copy this file to config/sender_vip_map (or set SENDER_VIP_MAPPINGS in .env)
# if you want to pin specific sender addresses to specific Outbound NAT VIPs.
#
# By default, any sender not listed here uses the dynamic VIP pool defined in .env:
#   randmap:{smtp_vip1,smtp_vip2,...} (or smtp_vip1 if only 1 VIP is configured)
# ==============================================================================
#
# Examples:
#
# 1. Isolate high-priority OTP emails to VIP 1 & VIP 2 (protects OTP IP reputation),
#    and route bulk notifications to other VIPs (e.g. VIP 3, VIP 4, VIP 5):
# otp@company.com           randmap:{smtp_vip1,smtp_vip2}
# notification@company.com  randmap:{smtp_vip3,smtp_vip4,smtp_vip5}
#
# 2. Pin a sender strictly to a single VIP (supports any configured VIP number vip1..vipN):
# otp@company.com           smtp_vip1:
# alerts@company.com        smtp_vip6:
